cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This is an independent historical-method reconstruction, not the original
  authors' source code. Cite the paper below for MLS, identify the software
  snapshot used in your work, and report its reconstruction assumptions and
  validation limits. The default saved-data first recommendation round is a
  documented failure, not a reproduction of the reported 80% efficiency.
title: "MSSM MLS historical reconstruction"
type: software
version: "0.1.1"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
authors:
  - name: "MSSM MLS reconstruction contributors"
abstract: >-
  An independent implementation of the Model-4 MSSM Machine Learning Scan
  described by Ren et al. (2019), using raw physical inputs and only natural-log
  relic-density labels. Includes explicit reconstruction assumptions and
  reproducible diagnostics of the default first-round failure. It is not
  recovered original author code or a verified reproduction of the paper's
  reported scan efficiency.
keywords:
  - MSSM
  - supersymmetry
  - machine learning scan
  - scientific reproducibility
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: Ren
      given-names: Jie
    - family-names: Wu
      given-names: Lei
    - family-names: Yang
      given-names: Jin Min
    - family-names: Zhao
      given-names: Jun
  title: "Exploring supersymmetry with machine learning"
  journal: "Nuclear Physics B"
  volume: "943"
  start: "114613"
  year: 2019
  doi: "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2019.114613"
  url: "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2019.114613"
